DSLR - Data Science ×Logistic Regression

Harry Potter and the Data Scientist

Objectives:

In this project Data Science ×Logistic Regression, you will continue your exploration of
Machine Learning by discovering dierent tools.
The use of the term Data Science in the title may be considered by some as excessive.
That is true. We do not claim to give you all the basics of Data Science in this topic.
The subject is vast. We will only cover some basics that we believe are useful for data
exploration before sending it to the machine learning algorithm.
You will implement a linear classication model as a continuation of the linear regres-
sion subject: a logistic regression. We also encourage you to create a machine learning
toolkit as you progress along the way.
Summarizing:
•You will learn how to read a data set, visualize it in dierent ways, and select and
clean unnecessary information from your data.
•You will train a logistic regression model that will solve a classification problem

Why use python?

Seemed like the logical choice to do data analysis, because its easy to code and has numerous libraries taht simly the calculations, the creation of matrix and the visualisation

Installation

Use the package manager pip to install all the libraries listed in requirements.txt
Use the following command: pip install -r requirements.txt

Data Analysis

describe.py is a program that can be called on both datasets, train and test, to get informations such as "mean", "min", "avg", "std", "25%", "50%", "75%", "max", "range", "variance" and "skewness". We use helper functions that we coded and can be found on the helper_functions folder

