1. Logisitic Regression Training

It is mandatory to use grandient descent to generate the weights for the prediction.

Gradient descent is an algorithm that numerically estimates where a function outputs its lowest values.

Our function f(x,y) defines defines an uneven surface. The gradient represents a slope. To find our minimum we can follow this slope little by little and repeat this operation enoguh times to get a result close enough to the optimum. The close we are to the minimum the lower the descent will be.

If the function has multiple local minimums, we may different results depending on our starting point.

Now what about logistic regression:
it is a supervised machine learning algorithm used for classification problems. (vs Linear regression which is used to predict continuous values)

Linear regression is used for binary classification where the output can either be 1 or 0. Sigmoid functions are used to convert inputs into a probability value between 0 and 1.

In our case we need to classify students between four of the Hogwart Houses, meaning we will need to use Multinomial Logisitic Regression.

